    <!-- privacy policy -->
    <string name="privacy_updated">Updated August 2026</string>
    <string name="privacy_h1">Your books stay yours</string>
    <string name="privacy_p1">A file you add to the library is copied into the app\'s private storage on your device. It is never uploaded anywhere, not even while you are signed in.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h2">Without an account, nothing leaves the device</string>
    <string name="privacy_p2">The whole app works signed out. In that state everything — progress, points, flashcards and settings — is kept on the device only.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h3">What is stored when you sign in</string>
    <string name="privacy_p3">With an account, these are held on Google Firebase servers: your name, email address, the profile picture and bio you wrote, your school, your reading progress, the classes you belong to, and what you hand in to them. That is what lets you carry on from the same place on another phone.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h4">Who can see it</string>
    <string name="privacy_p4">A teacher sees who joined their class, what was handed in, and the quiz results — for their own classes only. Students see each other\'s messages in the class stream. Nobody else sees anything.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h5">No adverts, no tracking</string>
    <string name="privacy_p5">There are no adverts, no analytics and no tracking of any kind in this app. Nothing is sold or passed to a third party.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h6">Deleting</string>
    <string name="privacy_p6">You can delete your account at any time from Settings. That removes the stored copy and the account itself. The books on your device remain yours.</string>
    <string name="privacy_h7">Crash reports</string>
    <string name="privacy_p7">If the app crashes, a report is written to your device and nowhere else. It is only sent if you choose to copy it and send it.</string>
</resources>
